      "title": "Qt: Don't call begin/endRetapPackets() twice",
      "message": "Qt: Don't call begin/endRetapPackets() twice\n\nAll the subclasses that inherit TapParameterDialog must implement\nfillTree(), and those that need to retap do so there (as a comment\ntowards the top of TapParameterDialog says.)\n\nThat means that cf_retap_packets() gets called, which means that\nthe callbacks that generate CaptureEvents for Retap Started and\nRetap Finish get generated in those functions, which means that\nWiresharkDialog (from which TapParameterDialog inherits) calls\nbeginRetapPackets() and endRetapPackets() anyway at appropriate\nmoments.\n\nTherefore, the TapParameterDialog doesn't need to call those\nexplicitly, because that calls them a second time. In particular,\nthe ServiceResponseTables (since 02b20a5a699a557ab0696ebb024b6a3b1d39c41e )\nadd the tables in endRetapPackets, and this means that every table\nis added twice. That isn't visible for dialogs that only have one\nsrt table, because of some extra tricks to hide the outer layer\nwhen there's only one table, but dialogs like SMB and NCP have extra\ntable entries.\n\nKeep that from happening by not calling endRetapPackets() twice.\n",
